{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>אחז</b> — four. Here and the other: אחז לאלעזר וגו׳ / אחז לאיתמר (I Chronicles), in the matter of the watches. חור כרפס ותכלת אחוז — because they were made into watches, thirty to stand over the song, they took one אחוז from the fifty. כרפס ותכלת אחוז — teaches that even though they were commanded to give only from yourselves, from man and beast, of their own accord they gave from the spoil of the movable property. We learn אחוז here from אחוז there."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The phrase 'הכא ואידך' refers to the four occurrences of the root אחז; the second and third are quoted from I Chronicles 24 and the fourth (חור כרפס ותכלת אחוז) appears to cite a different verse, possibly from a passage describing the temple musicians' garments or watches. The reading ל״ (thirty) is preserved as written; the connection between 'thirty to stand over the song' and the one-from-fifty levy is left as the author's terse hint."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:35.904357363Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}